

Hurrying through the rainswept November night, you're glad to see the bright lights of the Opera House. It's surprising that there aren't more people about but, hey, what do you expect in a cheap demo game...?

Cloak of Darkness
A basic IF demonstration.
Original game by Roger Firth
ZIL conversion by Jesse McGrew with bits and pieces by Jayson Smith
Additional material added for testing ZILF library by Josh Lawrence
Release 1 / Serial number 181205 / ZILF 0.8 lib J4

Foyer of the Opera House
You are standing in a spacious hall, splendidly decorated in red and gold, with glittering chandeliers overhead. The entrance from the street is to the north, and there are doorways south and west.

Stella is a brown corgi. She is in a deep sleep.

Bentley is a gray striped cat. He is in a deep sleep.

There is an apple, a painting, a table, a cube, and grime here.
On the table are grapes and a card.

> west
Did you know that the rug is a local-global object in the Foyer and the Bar?
Cloakroom
The walls of this small room were clearly once lined with hooks, though now only one remains. The exit is a door to the east, but there is also a cramped opening to the west.

A small brass hook is on the wall.

> west
You cannot enter the opening to the west while in possession of your cloak.

> drop cloak
You drop the cloak.

> west
Oof - it's cramped in here.
Hallway to Study
The hallway leads to a Study to the west, and back to the Cloakroom to the east.

A crude wooden sign hangs above the western exit.
A spider scuttles across your feet and then disappears into a crack.

> west
Study
A small room with a worn stand in the middle. A hallway lies east of here, a closet off to the west.

An ordinary light switch set in the wall beside the entrance to the closet.

A glass sphere.
In the sphere is a firefly.

A large glass case.
In the case is a muffin.

A cheap plastic flashlight.

There is a crate, a wallet, a safe, and a stand here.
On the stand are a book, a tray, and a jar.
A faint scratching sound can be heard from the ceiling.

> west
It is pitch black. You can't see a thing.

> east
Study

